     The MMDD55 module implements the RSA Data Security, Inc. MD5 Message-Digest
     Algorithm (MD5).  It produces 128-bit MD5 Digest of data.

     _M_D_5_I_n_i_t          must be called just before MMDD55TTrraannssffoorrmm() will be used
                      to produce a digest.  The _b_u_f argument is the storage
                      for the digest being produced on subsequent calls to the
                      MMDD55TTrraannssffoorrmm() routine.

     _M_D_5_T_r_a_n_s_f_o_r_m     is the core of the MD5 algorithm, this alters an exist‐
                      ing MD5 hash kept in _b_u_f to reflect the addition of 64
                      characters of new data passed in _b_l_o_c_k argument.

